{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideTarget","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideTarget","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Multiset.Sort","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.rskBurnside_imp_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.rskBurnside_imp_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBurnsideTarget.lean#L70-L78","doc":"**A proof of `RSKBurnsideHolds n` discharges the (deliberately weak) `RSK_substrate_axiom`.**\n`RSKBridge.RSK_substrate_axiom n` only asserts the *existence* of some `dimFn` with `∑ dimFn² = n!`\n(satisfiable trivially, hence not the real identity).  This theorem exhibits the genuine witness:\nonce `RSKBurnsideHolds n` is proved, `dimSYT` is exactly such a `dimFn`.  So the concrete identity is\nat least as strong as the abstract existential — the honest direction of the bridge.  (Stated with\nthe existential inline rather than importing `RSKBridge` to keep this file self-contained.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideHolds","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBurnsideTarget.lean#L60-L68","doc":"**Identity-I axiom (i), stated with the genuine SYT count** — the RSK / Burnside identity\n`∑_{p ⊢ n} dim(p)² = n!`.\n\nKept as a named `Prop` because a great deal of the corpus is phrased against it.  It is **no longer\nopen**: `QOU.Mathlib.rskBurnsideHolds` proves it for every `n` from the Robinson–Schensted\ncorrespondence, built in-repo since the pinned Mathlib lacks it.  This docstring previously said\n\"not yet a theorem … the multi-session next step\"; corrected 2026-08-23. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.dimSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.dimSYT","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBurnsideTarget.lean#L54-L58","doc":"The standard-tableau dimension of a partition: `#SYT` of its Young diagram.  This is the\ngenuine combinatorial `dim(p)` (a `Finite`-backed `Nat.card`), the concrete value the abstract\n`RSKBridge.RSKBijection.dim` field should carry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.partitionShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.partitionShape","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBurnsideTarget.lean#L49-L52","doc":"The Young diagram of a partition `p ⊢ n`: its parts, sorted weakly-decreasing, as row lengths\n(the same sorted list `PartitionListBridge.toList` produces). ","signatureChunk":0}]}